{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786430327,"nonce":"VHsIs3ex2XFFKSWgCf40dbnFJ8o=","message":"Caveat found after closing, worth knowing rather than reopening.\n\nThe harness reaps reliably when the test binary **exits normally**. It does not when the run is killed — several agent test runs were terminated mid-suite today and left **32 orphaned postgres:17-alpine containers** behind, which is the exact accumulation this issue describes. I removed them with `docker rm -f $(docker ps -aq --filter label=org.testcontainers=true)`, which is a safe one-liner because testcontainers labels its own and it cannot touch the compose stack or anything unrelated.\n\nThis is inherent to `TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_DISABLED`/socket-override setups: with ryuk absent, cleanup lives in `TerminateContainer` on the exit path, and SIGKILL does not run it. The one-container-per-binary template design keeps the blast radius small (32 rather than hundreds), so this is a papercut, not a regression of the fix.\n\nPossible follow-up if it bites again: add a `just test-clean` recipe wrapping that label-filtered prune, and mention it in the testing docs next to the colima note.","files":null}]}